### A YANG Module for Entitlement Inventory
* **Draft**: `draft-ietf-ivy-entitlement-inventory`
* **Presentation**: [A YANG Module for Entitlement Inventory](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-ivy-a-yang-module-for-entitlement-inventory-00)
* **Presenter**: Camilo Cardona

* **Discussion**:
  * **Revision -05 Updates**: Addressed YANG Doctor and Ops Directorate feedback with naming cleanups, type adjustments (`uint64`), and text clarifications.
  * **Data Integrity and Consistency**: Camilo Cardona explained that entitlement data can be inherently incomplete or inconsistent across devices and licensing systems. The model intentionally embraces reporting available entitlement state without attempting complex cross-system reconciliation.
  * **Capability Modeling & Post-Quantum Alignment**: Mahesh Jethanandani and Diego Lopez discussed linking entitlement capabilities with feature capabilities and Post-Quantum Cryptography (PQC) initiatives, noting alignment opportunities with the CADI draft (`draft-liu-cadi`).

